    <div class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-head" style="background:#eff6ff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><span style="font-size:18px">🎭</span><span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#1d4ed8">Layer 1 — Role Framing</span></div>
      <div class="guide-body">The prompt assigns the AI an expert identity calibrated to your org type. For nonprofits, it becomes an institutional fundraiser fluent in PCS taxonomy and foundation strategy. For for-profits, it becomes a grant consultant specializing in SBIR/STTR, federal R&D programs, and economic development funding. Research shows role framing significantly improves output vocabulary, analytical depth, and relevance.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-head" style="background:#fefce8;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><span style="font-size:18px">🧠</span><span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#854d0e">Layer 2 — Chain-of-Thought Reasoning</span></div>
      <div class="guide-body">The prompt instructs the AI to reason step by step: geography → eligibility → mission/market alignment → financial fit → access assessment → final ranking. This structured reasoning produces better prioritization than a simple list request, because the AI must justify each step before reaching conclusions.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-head" style="background:#f0fdf4;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><span style="font-size:18px">📊</span><span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#15803d">Layer 3 — Structured Output Format</span></div>
      <div class="guide-body">The prompt specifies an exact 9-column table with funder name, program, award range, deadline, where to find it, funding type, fit score, rationale, and flags. This prevents vague summaries and produces results you can immediately act on. After the table, it asks for funding categories, search keywords, and red flags.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-head" style="background:#fffbeb;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><span style="font-size:18px">✅</span><span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#92400e">Layer 4 — Verification &amp; Anti-Hallucination</span></div>
      <div class="guide-body">The AI is instructed to review its own list and remove any funder it is less than 80% confident about — 8 high-confidence matches beats 15 uncertain ones. Borderline entries get flagged with a specific thing to verify, protecting you from acting on fabricated information.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-card">
      <div class="guide-head" style="background:#f0fdf4;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><span style="font-size:18px">🏢</span><span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#065f46">For-Profit Mode — What's Different</span></div>
      <div class="guide-body">For-profit mode shifts the prompt to focus on non-dilutive government grants (SBIR/STTR, federal R&D agencies), state economic development programs, corporate innovation programs, and competition prizes. It adds NAICS code, TRL level, ownership certification, and dilution tolerance — all fields that gatekeep major government funding programs like SBIR Phase I/II.</div>
